      "id": 1,
      "text": "Jourdanton was founded in 1909 by Jourdan Campbell and his partner Colonel T.H., who saw the need for a railroad stop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.jourdantontexas.org/2173/History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s courthouse, originally built in 1909, was remodeled in 1956 to reflect the community’s progress.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/jourdanton-tx",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1910 the county seat moved from Pleasanton to Jourdanton, making it the administrative heart of Atascosa County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jourdanton%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
